TIP:  Those two notes that precede the first strum of (C) can be played two ways.  In the bass register form (C) but hover your ring finger over the open 5th string/2nd fret.  Pick the open <a> strings, place your finger down on the 2nd fret to cover the <b>, and then slide it up into the 3rd fret to strum (C).  In the treble register, for (C) but hover your middle finger over the open 3rd string/2nd fret.  Pick the open <a>, place your finger down on the 3rd string and pick the <b>, then lift and move the ring finger up one fret to complete and strum the (C).


